Subject: [qnx-porter 0001] wordsize-64
Source: deterministic rule
Reason: The library guesses the word size from glibc's __WORDSIZE, else from __x86_64__, else assumes 32 bits (cmocka.h), and so redefines (u)intptr_t as a 32-bit type on aarch64. QNX 8.0's x86_64 and aarch64le targets are both LP64 and QNX's headers never define __WORDSIZE, so define it as 64.
Error: /home/chirag/qnx-porter/ports-aarch64le/cmocka/work/src/include/cmocka.h:137:28: error: conflicting types for 'uintptr_t'; have 'unsigned int'
---
--- a/qnx-toolchain.cmake
+++ b/qnx-toolchain.cmake
@@ -13,8 +13,8 @@
 set(CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH_MODE_LIBRARY ONLY)
 set(CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH_MODE_INCLUDE ONLY)
 # -g: debug info only (same code), so a crash on the target gives file:line in its backtrace
-set(CMAKE_C_FLAGS_INIT "-g ")
-set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_INIT "-g ")
+set(CMAKE_C_FLAGS_INIT "-g -D__WORDSIZE=64")
+set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_INIT "-g -D__WORDSIZE=64")
 set(CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS_INIT "-L/home/chirag/qnx-porter/ports-aarch64le/cmocka/work/stubs")
 set(CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS_INIT "-L/home/chirag/qnx-porter/ports-aarch64le/cmocka/work/stubs")
 # Flags after the project's own (appended by the compiler wrappers in -): none
